ture":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I've gathered comprehensive data from multiple scientific sources. Now I'll compile the results into a structured JSON file:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_85e8107eddd44fc8aa03d795","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"{\n  \"osint_crawl_results\": {\n    \"query\": \"alkylamines\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-02-18T22:08:00+05:30\",\n    \"total_sources_crawled\": 4,\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"source_id\": 1,\n        \"title\": \"Amine\",\n        \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amine\",\n        \"source_type\": \"encyclopedia\",\n        \"content_snippet\": \"In chemistry, amines are organic compounds that contain carbon–nitrogen bonds. Amines are formed when one or more hydrogen atoms in ammonia are replaced by alkyl or aryl groups. The nitrogen atom in an amine possesses a lone pair of electrons. Amines can also exist as heterocyclic compounds. Aniline is the simplest aromatic amine.\",\n        \"classification\": \"Primary (1°), Secondary (2°), Tertiary (3°) amines; Aliphatic vs Aromatic amines; Cyclic amines\",\n        \"key_concepts\": [\n          \"Functional group -NH2 in primary amines\",\n          \"General formulas: RNH2 (primary), R2NH (secondary), R3N (tertiary)\",\n          \"Aliphatic amines contain only H and alkyl substituents\",\n          \"Aromatic amines have nitrogen connected to aromatic ring\",\n          \"Cyclic amines include aziridine, piperidine\"\n        ],\n        \"examples\": [\n          \"Methylamine (primary alkyl amine)\",\n          \"Dimethylamine (secondary alkyl amine)\",\n          \"Trimethylamine (tertiary alkyl amine)\",\n          \"Aniline (aromatic amine)\",\n          \"Tris (buffering agent)\"\n        ],\n        \"outbound_links\": [\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methylamine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimethylamine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trimethylamine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aniline\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aromatic_amine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aziridine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piperidine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EDTA\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": 2,\n        \"title\": \"Psychotropic alkylamines\",\n        \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychotropic_alkylamines\",\n        \"source_type\": \"encyclopedia_specialized\",\n        \"content_snippet\": \"Psychotropic alkylamines are alkylamines that share the critical property of not containing an aromatic nucleus, but are still biologically active. While many of these molecules are stimulants, others are antiviral, have competitive NMDA antagonist activity, or are nicotinic receptor antagonists.\",\n        \"key_concepts\": [\n          \"Biologically active alkylamines without aromatic nucleus\",\n          \"NMDA receptor antagonists\",\n          \"Antiviral properties\",\n          \"Sympathomimetic effects\",\n          \"Catecholamine release\"\n        ],\n        \"compounds_table\": [\n          {\n            \"compound\": \"Neramexane\",\n            \"core\": \"Cyclohexyl\",\n            \"substituent\": \"1,3,3,5,5-Pentamethyl\",\n            \"n_substituent\": \"1-NH2\",\n            \"pharmacology\": \"NMDA receptor antagonist\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"compound\": \"Amantadine\",\n            \"core\": \"adamantane\",\n            \"substituent\": \"-\",\n            \"n_substituent\": \"1-NH2\",\n            \"pharmacology\": \"antiviral, NMDA antagonist, catecholamine releaser, cholinergic\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"compound\": \"Memantine\",\n            \"core\": \"-\",\n            \"substituent\": \"3,5-DiMe\",\n            \"n_substituent\": \"-\",\n            \"pharmacology\": \"NMDA antagonist\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"compound\": \"Rimantadine\",\n            \"core\": \"-\",\n            \"substituent\": \"CH3CH\",\n            \"n_substituent\": \"NH2\",\n            \"pharmacology\": \"antiviral\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"compound\": \"Cyclopentamine\",\n            \"core\": \"cyclopentane\",\n            \"substituent\": \"n-propyl\",\n            \"n_substituent\": \"2-NHMe\",\n            \"pharmacology\": \"Sympathomimetic vasoconstrictor\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"outbound_links\": [\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neramexane\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amantadine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memantine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rimantadine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclopentamine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Propylhexedrine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methylhexanamine\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuaminoheptane\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychotropic\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aromaticity\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": 3,\n        \"title\": \"Amines\",\n        \"url\": \"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Amine\",\n        \"source_type\": \"scientific_database\",\n        \"content_snippet\": \"Amine is a class of organic compounds that contain nitrogen as the pivotal atom for functional groups. A group of compounds derived from ammonia by substituting organic radicals for the hydrogens. PubChem CID: 139106940\",\n        \"chemical_properties\": {\n          \"molecular_formula\": \"C30H58N6\",\n          \"molecular_weight\": \"502.8 g/mol\",\n          \"computed_by\": \"PubChem 2.2 (PubChem release 2025.09.15)\",\n          \"parent_compound\": \"CID 14423437 (2,3-Dicyclohexyl-1,1-dimethylguanidine)\",\n          \"synonyms\": [\n            \"Substituted amine\",\n            \"RefChem:388790\",\n            \"CHEBI:32952\",\n            \"691-275-1\",\n            \"amine\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"available_representations\": [\n          \"2D Structure\",\n          \"3D Conformer\",\n          \"Crystal Structures\"\n        ],\n        \"crystal_data\": {\n          \"cod_number\": \"4078087\",\n          \"space_group\": \"P 1 21/c 1\",\n          \"lattice_parameters\": {\n            \"a\": \"9.6674 Å\",\n            \"b\": \"16.4856 Å\",\n            \"c\": \"21.5869 Å\",\n            \"α\": \"90.00 °\",\n            \"β\": \"114.389 °\",\n            \"γ\": \"90.00 °\"\n          },\n          \"Z\": \"8\",\n          \"Z'\": \"2\",\n          \"residual_factor\": \"0.0415\"\n        },\n        \"outbound_links\": [\n          \"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/element/Nitrogen\",\n          \"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Guanidine\",\n          \"https://www.crystallography.net/cod/4078087.html\",\n          \"http://doi.org/10.1021/om300097a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": 4,\n        \"title\": \"Search results for alkylamines\",\n        \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=alkylamines\",\n        \"source_type\": \"research_portal\",\n        \"content_snippet\": \"PubMed search returned 1,894 results for alkylamines across 190 pages. Recent research includes photoinduced reactions, electrochemical synthesis, catalytic C-H activation, and analytical methods for alkylamines.\",\n        \"total_results\": 1894,\n        \"total_pages\": 190,\n        \"recent_research_highlights\": [\n          {\n            \"title\": \"Photoinduced alpha-Aminoalkylation of Sulfonylarenes with Alkylamines\",\n            \"authors\": \"Yonekura K, et al.\",\n            \"journal\": \"Chemistry\",\n            \"year\": 2023,\n            \"pmid\": \"37681494\",\n            \"snippet\": \"Photoinduced alpha-aminoalkylation of sulfonylarenes with alkylamines was found to be induced by photoirradiation. Various types of alkylamines are applicable including trialkylamines, dialkylamines, N,N-dialkylanilines and N-alkylanilines.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"title\": \"Multicomponent Construction of Tertiary Alkylamines by Photoredox/Nickel-Catalyzed Aminoalkylation\",\n            \"authors\": \"Yang T, et al.\",\n            \"journal\": \"J Am Chem Soc\",\n            \"year\": 2024,\n            \"pmid\": \"39394998\",\n            \"snippet\": \"Tertiary alkylamines are privileged structural motifs widely present in natural products, pharmaceutical agents, and bioactive molecules. The functionalization of alpha-amino radicals derived from alkylamines enables efficient synthesis.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"title\": \"Catalytic C(sp(3))-H bond activation in tertiary alkylamines\",\n            \"authors\": \"Rodrigalvarez J, et al.\",\n            \"journal\": \"Nat Chem\",\n            \"year\": 2020,\n            \"pmid\": \"31863014\",\n            \"snippet\": \"The development of robust catalytic methods to assemble tertiary alkylamines provides a continual challenge. Transformation of traditionally unreactive C-H bonds proximal to the nitrogen atom into versatile chemical entities.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"title\": \"The state of art on the analysis of alkylamines in atmospheric particulate matter\",\n            \"authors\": \"Nuckowski Ł.\",\n            \"journal\": \"J Chromatogr A\",\n            \"year\": 2025,\n            \"pmid\": \"40684665\",\n            \"snippet\": \"Alkylamines, despite being volatile compounds, are ubiquitous components of atmospheric particulate matter due to their ability to form salts via acid-base reactions. Recent research highlights the importance of alkylamine speciation.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"title\": \"Evaluation of alkylamines and stationary phases to improve LC-MS of oligonucleotides\",\n            \"authors\": \"Bartlett MG, et al.\",\n            \"journal\": \"Biomed Chromatogr\",\n            \"year\": 2021,\n            \"pmid\": \"33283300\",\n            \"snippet\": \"The BEH C(18), peptide, and phenyl columns were capable of providing significant retention of oligonucleotide samples across multiple ion-pairing systems using alkylamines and HFIP.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"outbound_links\": [\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37681494/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32432808/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37675955/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39394998/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33283300/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31863014/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40684665/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38885646/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34543004/\",\n          \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38408428/\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"overview\": \"Alkylamines are a fundamental class of organic compounds characterized by carbon-nitrogen bonds where hydrogen atoms in ammonia are replaced by alkyl groups. They serve as crucial building blocks in pharmaceuticals, natural products, and industrial chemistry.\",\n      \"key_findings\": [\n        \"Classification: Primary (RNH2), secondary (R2NH), tertiary (R3N) amines based on substitution\",\n        \"Aliphatic amines contain only alkyl groups, while aromatic amines connect to aromatic rings\",\n        \"Cyclic amines (aziridines, piperidines) represent important structural variants\",\n        \"Psychotropic alkylamines exhibit biological activity without aromatic nuclei, including NMDA antagonists like amantadine and memantine\",\n        \"Recent research focuses on photoinduced and electrochemical synthesis methods for alkylamines\",\n        \"Catalytic C-H activation near nitrogen remains a significant synthetic challenge\",\n        \"Alkylamines play important roles in atmospheric chemistry and analytical methods\"\n      ],\n      \"research_trends\": [\n        \"Photoredox catalysis for alkylamine functionalization\",\n        \"Electrochemical arylation methods\",\n        \"Multicomponent reactions for tertiary alkylamine synthesis\",\n        \"Environmental analysis of alkylamines in particulate matter\",\n        \"LC-MS method development using alkylamine additives\"\n      ],\n      \"useful_outbound_links\": [\n        \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amine (Comprehensive classification)\",\n        \"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Amine (Chemical properties & structures)\",\n        \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=alkylamines (Latest research papers)\",\n        \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychotropic_alkylamines (Biological activities)\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-osint\\alkylamines_osint_results.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":33094,"output":3759,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":36853,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771432806854}}
